      "text": "The total surface area of the pyramid consists of the area of the square base and the area of the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the square base:**\n\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = \\text{side length}^2 = 10^2 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of one triangular face:**\n\n   Each triangle is an isosceles triangle with a base of 10 cm and a height of 12 cm (since the peak is 12 cm above the center of the base).\n\n   First, we find the height of the triangular face using the Pythagorean theorem. The height from the center of the base to the midpoint of one of the base edges (the height of the isosceles triangle) can be found by considering a right triangle formed by half the diagonal of the square base, the height of the triangle, and the slant height of the pyramid.\n\n   The diagonal of the square base is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Diagonal} = \\text{side length} \\times \\sqrt{2} = 10\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n   Half of the diagonal is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\text{Diagonal}}{2} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{2} = 5\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n   Using the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle formed by the height of the pyramid, the height of the triangular face, and half the diagonal:\n   \\[\n   h_{\\text{triangular face}}^2 + (5\\sqrt{2})^2 = 12^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   h_{\\text{triangular face}}^2 + 50 = 144\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   h_{\\text{triangular face}}^2 = 94\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   h_{\\text{triangular face}} = \\sqrt{94}\n   \\]\n\n   The area of one triangular face is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times \\sqrt{94} = 5\\sqrt{94} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n   Since there are four triangular faces, the total area of the triangular faces is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the triangular faces} = 4 \\times 5\\sqrt{94} = 20\\sqrt{94} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total surface area of the pyramid:**\n\n   The total surface area is the sum of the area of the base and the area of the four triangular faces:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = \\text{Area of the base} + \\text{Total area of the triangular faces} = 100 + 20\\sqrt{94}\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, the total surface area of the pyramid is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{100 + 20\\sqrt{94}}\n   \\]",
